{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And Aharon's sons Nadav and Avihu took — before the fire went out from before YHWH they had already each taken his fire-pan to burn incense inside, on the golden altar, for the morning incense precedes the limbs. And they put in them alien fire, which He had not commanded them — Moshe did not command and did not want them to bring ordinary fire on this day, because even though on other days it is written ונתנו בני אהרן הכהן אש על המזבח, today they were expecting the descent of supernal fire, and it was not good on this day to bring this, in order to sanctify the Name of Heaven so that all would know that fire comes from heaven — as Elijah said — ואש לא תשימו, because He wanted to sanctify the Name of Heaven through the descent of fire from above."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The lemma cited by the standard text (ואש לא תשימו) does not match Elijah's words in 1 Kings 18; the reference and its connection are textually unclear and translated hyper-literally as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:30.677367514Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}